---

## What We Are Building

Autonomous AI animation factory (Next.js + Inngest + Supabase, local Windows). This
session: (1) recovered/finished **episode E27** through final cut + distribution;
(2) ran a **stability audit** (why any server/task glitch leaves statuses stuck) and
executed its #1 fix — **self-host durable Inngest**; (3) fixed a batch of E27-tail bugs
(stitch ENOENT, composer-centric music, final-cut drawer, copywriter model); (4) designed
a unified **kebab colour grammar** (approved, not yet implemented).

---

## What WORKED (with evidence)

- **Self-host durable Inngest (Tier-0 fix)** — `inngest start` (durable SQLite, no
  Docker/Postgres/Redis) replaces `inngest dev`. Confirmed: killed inngest → restarted on
  same `--sqlite-dir` → reloaded from `main.db` (156KB on disk, :8288→200); app re-synced
  `{"message":"Successfully registered"}`. Prod signing mode: `[inngest] Using native Web
  Crypto for request signing`. Memory `inngest_selfhost_setup.md` + CLAUDE.md §13.
- **E27 shipped** — VID-final_cut **v02 APPROVED**; stitch COMPLETED twice (13:56, 13:59)
  after the ENOENT deploy (3 prior FAILED with ENOENT before the fix). Distribution ran
  auto → uploaded UNLISTED to YouTube.
- **Stitch ENOENT fix** — `runner.ts` loadBytes demotes a `/api/media|/staging` URL sitting
  in `staging_path` instead of `fs.readFile`-ing it (was `C:\api\media\…mp3` ENOENT). Root
  data fix: `ingest-music.ts` writes `staging_path: null` (not the URL). Verified: tsc·0,
  vitest 1210, replay-pilot 30/30, and E27 stitch actually succeeded post-deploy.
- **Composer-centric music** — AUD-music got Approve in the drawer; approving bakes into the
  animatic (`bakeMusicIntoEpisodeAnimatic` helper + `computeNextEvents` AUD-music branch);
  timeline Replace/Upload removed. Verified tsc·0 / vitest 1210 / replay 30.
- **Final-cut drawer** — VID-final_cut now shows version picker + Approve (reuse
  CandidatesStrip + PilotApproveButtons). Live in prod.
- **Copywriter fix** — Haiku→Sonnet 4.6 + hard rule "title = final headline only" (Haiku had
  echoed the prompt's principle into the published title). Live. tsc·0.
- **4 deploys** all clean (build exit 0, app 200) via stop→rm .next→build→start.
- **Git**: master `37eb7b7` (E27-tail fixes) + `b99a59f` (start-stack + CLAUDE.md §13), both
  pushed to origin.

---

## What Did NOT Work (and why)

- **Cleaning the 3 zombie jobs / re-firing paid VGEN via script** — the auto-mode classifier
  BLOCKED every prod-mutation script (marking jobs FAILED, sending inngest events) 3×,
  demanding direct Director approval. Read-only probes were fine. Workaround: Director drove
  the remaining video via UI clicks; the videos completed that way.
- **`inngest dev` (the old setup)** — root cause of the whole day's pain: it's ephemeral
  in-memory; it DIED silently at 10:58:45Z and stayed dead ~2h, so `inngest.send` failed
  ("fetch failed", swallowed) and 3 mid-flight jobs stayed RUNNING forever (zombies). Fixed
  by self-host. This is why the Director's "generate video" clicks did nothing until revival.
- **Inngest Cloud (considered, set aside)** — needs the app publicly reachable (it pushes to
  /api/inngest); app is localhost + local ffmpeg → self-host fits better. Cloud free tier
  likely fits (~190 runs/episode from E27) but concurrency/retention are the real caps.

---

