## Decisions Made

- **Tier-0 = self-host Inngest, minimal (SQLite, no Docker/Postgres/Redis)** — Director:
  "минимальная конфигурация подойдёт, падает редко только на батчах." Cloud needs public
  app reachability; self-host fits the local ffmpeg/localhost setup and is $0.
- **Copywriter → Sonnet 4.6** (from Haiku) — Haiku echoed prompt principles into the title.
- **Music is composer-centric** — refs-landscape ≠ video-output-landscape; ONE upload place
  (composer), approve→timeline auto, no Replace button.
- **E27 stays 16:9** — refs landscape (gpt-image-2 can't do true 9:16); shorts by crop later.
  Backlog: shorts-derivation (auto-reframe/crop-safe master) + delivery-target aspect fix.
- **Discussion vs code split** — Director uses a separate terminal at `C:\SandyStudio` for
  read-only discussion/research; THIS session owns code+deploy+running servers.

---

## Blockers & Open Questions

- **Auto-classifier blocks all prod mutations** (job cleanup, paid re-fire) → need Director
  `go`/UI. This is friction; the reaper (Tier-1) removes the need for manual zombie cleanup.
- **Distribution copy already published** with the bad title (Director editing on YouTube);
  the Sonnet fix prevents recurrence next episode.
- **Inngest Cloud free-tier exact numbers** — Director verifying in the discussion terminal
  (moot for now since we chose self-host).

---

## Exact Next Step

**Audit Tier-1 quick wins** (fresh session, pipeline idle): start with the two highest-leverage,
lowest-risk: (1) add a factory-level `onFailure` handler that flips the job row to FAILED +
releases the dispatch claim (reuse `markJobFailed` / `markDispatchIntent`); (2) an out-of-band
stale-RUNNING reaper (NOT an inngest function). Then the 2-file provider-timeout finish
(anthropic-brief/vision) + the 1-line critic-loop `logEvent` HALT. These make the jobs table
self-healing even with the durable executor and retire the 3 zombies + the classifier friction.

